{"title":"Nesbitt's Inequality","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Nesbitt's <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inequality\" title=\"Inequality\">Inequality</a></b> is a theorem which, although rarely cited, has many instructive proofs.  It states that for positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57e6bbafc674a9b5a5fc63694cd7a4190f69eed5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b+c} + \\frac{b}{c+a} + \\frac{c}{a+b} \\ge \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"209\" height=\"39\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>with equality when all the variables are equal.\n</p><p>All of the proofs below generalize to prove the following more general inequality.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75bc11e2f2868b7a188f6ebd8b0b2485414112cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, \\ldots a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"11\" /> are positive and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e93a160eff9bb47dbb0f80f0b790fce2d767c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{n}a_i = s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"78\" height=\"53\" />, then \n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9bba5a3a6ab6292521575edac5fd074000d3bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\frac{a_i}{s-a_i} \\geq \\frac{n}{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"147\" height=\"48\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>or equivalently\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96aa329d97fea714fc60c123219562a584926441.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\frac{s}{s-a_i} \\geq \\frac{n^2}{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"147\" height=\"48\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>with equality when all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> are equal.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Proofs\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proofs</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#By_Smoothing\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">By Smoothing</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#By_Rearrangement\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">By Rearrangement</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#By_Cauchy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">By Cauchy</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#By_AM-GM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">By AM-GM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#By_Expansion_and_AM-GM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">By Expansion and AM-GM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-3 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#By_AM-HM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">By AM-HM</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#By_Substitution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">By Substitution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#By_Normalization_and_AM-HM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">By Normalization and AM-HM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#By_Weighted_AM-HM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">By Weighted AM-HM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#By_Muirhead&#39;s_and_Cauchy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">By Muirhead's and Cauchy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Another_Interesting_Method\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Another Interesting Method</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#By_Muirhead&#39;s_and_expansion\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">By Muirhead's and expansion</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proofs\">Proofs</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proofs\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"By_Smoothing\">By Smoothing</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: By Smoothing\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We may normalize so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/6/0463a97b25dc0b519ce3c0a1ba6ff2ab6f9f518f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />. Then we wish to show<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15ee2d0fe6a0fe7cd600c5de5aa0784897b1939b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a}{1-a}+\\frac{b}{1-b}+\\frac{c}{1-c}\\geq\\frac32.\\]\" width=\"214\" height=\"38\" />The equality case is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566b9136144a62fac113ecbc8065793a74123238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=c$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" /> so we can use smoothing. We wish to show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28f3af31db9f75b43a71305c80e94f5dbc5891cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\neq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> then<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04db5a404781383ee01113fc1833955e4caeff6a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a}{1-a}+\\frac{b}{1-b}&gt;2\\cdot\\frac{\\frac{a+b}2}{1-\\frac{a+b}2}.\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"48\" />If this is true, then if the minimum occurs at a point where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28f3af31db9f75b43a71305c80e94f5dbc5891cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\neq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> then we can replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> with their average and then the expression decreases, so that cannot be the minimum. Thus the minimum occurs where they are all equal, and we would be done.\n</p><p>Expanding both sides of the inequality and clearing denominators we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601781ea36bf25253a639065afdb9ea45f97db00.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2+b^2&gt;2ab,\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />which is true because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28f3af31db9f75b43a71305c80e94f5dbc5891cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\neq b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"By_Rearrangement\">By Rearrangement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: By Rearrangement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d498e24e074976fca72993a9778707f8a57218c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{b+c} = \\frac{1}{a+b+c -a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"170\" height=\"38\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/011cae95a7490bc452c3227eb3c2db468bc0e4ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{c+a} = \\frac{1}{a+b+c -b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"170\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d7b04765f2079bcb9484a2b2f89fc3c3ec1d4d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a+b} = \\frac{1}{a+b+c -c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"170\" height=\"38\" /> are sorted in the same order.  Then by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rearrangement_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rearrangement inequality\">rearrangement inequality</a>,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/8/948de263472a7346289d108e5a34d27345d4a773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\left( \\frac{a}{b+c} + \\frac{b}{c+a} + \\frac{c}{a+b} \\right) \\ge \\frac{b}{b+c} + \\frac{c}{b+c} + \\frac{c}{c+a} + \\frac{a}{c+a} + \\frac{a}{a+b} + \\frac{b}{a+b} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"638\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>For equality to occur, since we changed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/6/52666bc8a6f62434e3d8f7f351f3430fb5a88d60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} a \\cdot \\frac{1}{b+c} + b \\cdot \\frac{1}{c+a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"150\" height=\"38\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d3baa25a63d72a4f8d4659196fb5a24a2a336ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\cdot \\frac{1}{b+c} + a \\cdot \\frac{1}{c+a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"150\" height=\"38\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, so by symmetry, all the variables must be equal.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"By_Cauchy\">By Cauchy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: By Cauchy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cauchy-Schwarz_Inequality\" title=\"Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality\">Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality</a>, we have\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/5/5b5ea4ee53b7d8a89e70aa883da27dbc7b095114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[(b+c) + (c+a) + (a+b)]\\left( \\frac{1}{b+c} + \\frac{1}{c+a} + \\frac{1}{a+b} \\right) \\geq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"449\" height=\"43\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>or\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bda51d00d4e6e0f104ed58d68d8b9b79ac765c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\left( \\frac{a+b+c}{b+c} + \\frac{a+b+c}{c+a} + \\frac{a+b+c}{a+b} \\right) \\geq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"336\" height=\"43\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>as desired.  Equality occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/9/729d92b8c5dcb4445c47c6c2999a28eaf78f2633.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b+c)^2 = (c+a)^2 = (a+b)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"229\" height=\"19\" />, i.e., when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566b9136144a62fac113ecbc8065793a74123238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=c$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>We also present three closely related variations of this proof, which illustrate how <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-HM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-HM\">AM-HM</a> is related to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a> and Cauchy.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"By_AM-GM\">By AM-GM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: By AM-GM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>By applying <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a> twice, we have\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9da2c9ba82d2b427838486c39738002cf0b2cee1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[(b+c) + (c+a) + (a+b)] \\left( \\frac{1}{b+c} + \\frac{1}{c+a} + \\frac{1}{a+b} \\right) \\geq 3 [(b+c)(c+a)(a+b)]^{\\frac{1}{3}} \\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{(b+c)(c+a)(a+b)}\\right)^{\\frac{1}{3}} = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"876\" height=\"49\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>which yields the desired inequality.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"By_Expansion_and_AM-GM\">By Expansion and AM-GM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: By Expansion and AM-GM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>We consider the equivalent inequality\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/2/6f2f086a2bfc1610b038f7fa0eb5a9efd8ff07fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[(b+c) + (c+a) + (a+c)]\\left( \\frac{1}{b+c} + \\frac{1}{c+a} + \\frac{1}{a+b} \\right) \\geq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"450\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/9650a482a74885220ea5976c502c025799edaa8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = b+c, y= c+a, z= a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"235\" height=\"16\" />, we expand the left side to obtain\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec60e447efac1ce3be80a89dba47c83f0e444ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + \\frac{x}{y} + \\frac{y}{x} + \\frac{y}{z} + \\frac{z}{y} + \\frac{z}{x} + \\frac{x}{z} \\geq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"260\" height=\"36\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>which follows from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/b/3db6b548bf4a585371752f7f500f2121c37327f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y} + \\frac{y}{x} \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"83\" height=\"36\" />, etc., by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a>, with equality when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/1/3a1bb32241472c525e5624db47ff8edf81dd33a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p>\n<h4><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"By_AM-HM\">By AM-HM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: By AM-HM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h4>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-HM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-HM\">AM-HM</a> inequality for three variables,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/d/ead23fce27d2395c7b46b09af9e03dfec84d9e4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+y+z}{3} \\geq \\frac{3}{\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"182\" height=\"46\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>is equivalent to\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f19d2b4344b3d4dd2268a746c1ee7c5442533992.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+y+z) \\left(\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{z}\\right) \\geq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"235\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/5/e559cb8a181d583d4da68d93ed5d039769e5e5d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=b+c, y=c+a, z=a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"235\" height=\"16\" /> yields the desired inequality.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"By_Substitution\">By Substitution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: By Substitution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6ad673859f911fc1e678e17a601bc561ee28a2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{a}{b+c}, y = \\frac{b}{c+a}, z = \\frac{c}{a+b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"245\" height=\"39\" /> satisfy the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9d8fc8befc29ff5ba5cee7f5142bbd12ebbb0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy + yz + zx + 2xyz = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"195\" height=\"15\" />.  Thus it is sufficient to prove that if any numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9d8fc8befc29ff5ba5cee7f5142bbd12ebbb0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy + yz + zx + 2xyz = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"195\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/3/e430c488252432f759acd39a2a29bd451dd9e562.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z \\geq \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"109\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose, on the contrary, that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5da34af67ea4af72e92c731fda8352b8ddf8064.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z &lt; \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"109\" height=\"37\" />.  We then have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/7/db737396ec9e23587a79d2c0d16e0dc5e5d9f980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy + yz + zx \\leq \\frac{(x+y+z)^2}{3} &lt; \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"262\" height=\"39\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a95c6d211c6c3b43fb5623edeb1075f16b2b4047.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2xyz \\leq 2 \\left( \\frac{x+y+z}{3} \\right)^3 &lt; \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"225\" height=\"48\" />.  Adding these inequalities yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/b/ddb99f5db1ea222717b4ff49713be83dd748e5ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy + yz + zx + 2xyz &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"195\" height=\"15\" />, a contradiction.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"By_Normalization_and_AM-HM\">By Normalization and AM-HM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: By Normalization and AM-HM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We may normalize so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec972889b44f27273e420e9d5228d95ff7e65407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />.  It is then sufficient to prove\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/e/21e98106e719f81c9de5e6f56dc917e6df808cc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{b+c} + \\frac{1}{c+a} + \\frac{1}{a+b} \\geq \\frac{9}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"209\" height=\"39\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>which follows from <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-HM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-HM\">AM-HM</a>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"By_Weighted_AM-HM\">By Weighted AM-HM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: By Weighted AM-HM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We may normalize so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1c28abcb3f07b7c5d671820f24064f034f3e322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c =1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We first note that by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rearrangement_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rearrangement inequality\">rearrangement inequality</a> or the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1ce9f8a96846e98d4ccc76eb54340994b101f29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-b)^2 + (b-c)^2 + (c-a)^2 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"262\" height=\"21\" />,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96ce4257bce9994a87f1ae0014372229a8bc5bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 (ab + bc + ca) \\leq a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + 2(ab + bc + ca)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"373\" height=\"19\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>so\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/70620c204f4a2729ebe991873cbd81122541045f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a(b+c) + b(c+a) + c(a+b)} \\geq \\frac{1}{\\frac{2}{3}(a+b+c)^2} = \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"399\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec972889b44f27273e420e9d5228d95ff7e65407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />, weighted AM-HM gives us\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/95752a7be4a5647287a40e2c8632c570fb0e0750.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cdot \\frac{1}{b+c} + b \\cdot \\frac{1}{c+a} + c \\cdot \\frac{1}{a+b} \\geq \\frac{1}{a(b+c) + b(c+a) + c(a+b)} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"531\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<h3><span id=\"By_Muirhead.27s_and_Cauchy\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"By_Muirhead's_and_Cauchy\">By Muirhead's and Cauchy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: By Muirhead&#39;s and Cauchy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>By Cauchy, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52eb15a3738556cbf19a5594cb2cefcb383752b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{\\text{cyc}}\\frac{a^2}{ab + ac} \\geq \\frac{(a + b + c)^2}{2(ab + ac + bc)} = \\frac{a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + 2(ab + ac + bc)}{2(ab + ac + bc)}\\]\" width=\"495\" height=\"48\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/a/c3a7c8871be738dfae6b35115e4f7c507d6bdda0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= 1 + \\frac{a^2 + b^2 + c^2}{2(ab + ac + bc)} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"43\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afd47c5b59dc0d9bb0070f15360edec7fb9d7311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 + c^2 \\geq ab + ac + bc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"213\" height=\"19\" /> by Muirhead as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/294d7d4a0e155105c3542451a00e3d07a6d280b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[1, 1, 0]\\prec [2, 0, 0]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Another_Interesting_Method\">Another Interesting Method</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Another Interesting Method\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/3/f03dbbc6fb369b18af35eadebd617497a4bf8482.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S=\\frac{a}{b+c}+\\frac{b}{c+a}+\\frac{c}{a+b}\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"39\" />\nAnd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/9/e39400ceecc8781d935fd53ed9fdcb0ce1147dbd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M=\\frac{b}{b+c}+\\frac{c}{c+a}+\\frac{a}{a+b}\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"39\" />\nAnd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc46101d455cf78f940a2c4f8694ea91bbbe9fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N=\\frac{c}{b+c}+\\frac{a}{c+a}+\\frac{b}{a+b}\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"39\" />\nNow, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a351fb585d82ed20cc0389a627244246d3ce8a94.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M+N=3\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />\nAlso by AM-GM; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8e075904e01d4f9d4a1bbcc290cbfc0f8e5bde.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M+S\\geq 3\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d6657b199ed99cd26d1049daee02197f82302e52.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N+S\\geq 3\\]\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b26ce3289de14caa07ab2a8cb970d774398a7542.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies M+N+2S\\geq 6\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e41bc2528e9d95a926288a3ea699c75441ca5117.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 2S\\geq 3\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a09fc9eae42e4c03b51623a004ee2a33e514f382.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies S\\geq \\frac{3}{2}\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"By_Muirhead.27s_and_expansion\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"By_Muirhead's_and_expansion\">By Muirhead's and expansion</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nesbitt%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: By Muirhead&#39;s and expansion\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114068fd2fc7a324ccede2320eeabdb947645082.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[x,y,z]=\\sum_{sym} a^xb^yc^z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"156\" height=\"40\" />. Expanding out we get that our inequality is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/e/ebeb82455310c92d99ac35070bbdb80233ce6b68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{cyc} a^3+\\sum_{sym} a^2b+\\sum_{cyc} abc \\geq \\frac{3(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)}{2}\\]\" width=\"392\" height=\"48\" /> This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/41663bc4a36377b0052c9e0d8058896394b7f865.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[3,0,0]/2+[2,1,0]+[1,1,1]/2\\geq \\frac{3}{2}(a+b)(b+c)(a+c)\\]\" width=\"434\" height=\"37\" /> So it follows that we must prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299939a80241b575b5b1fb07af4f5b3288db3ce7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[3,0,0]+2[2,1,0]+[1,1,1]\\geq 3([2,1,0]+[1,1,1]/3)\\]\" width=\"405\" height=\"18\" /> So it follows that we must prove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a34cc571bf298fbb2aaff9e17e553b7688c2e1f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[3,0,0]\\geq [2,1,0]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"20\" /> which immediately follows from Muirhead's.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018035632\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 404/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14981/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4904:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018035632 and revision id 179434. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}